## Misconceptions and correction

Signs: calling F^X−F^Y basis; labeling negative B backwardation; calling all shorts borrowed assets; assuming convergence predicts a smooth fall. Correction: label each price before subtraction; endpoint argument compares executable trades on the same deliverable. Hint1: basis includes spot. Hint2: plug S into S−F. O006-C1 / v1: S40,F^X45,F^Y43. Find B,D and say whether this is the lecture's normal contango. Key B−5,D+2, contango for X but not normal contango because later43<earlier45. Pass both gaps and rejected ordering; partial missing reason; fail wrong comparator.

The sign alone is a tentative diagnosis; use the learner's reasoning to establish the confusion. Score the initial response before any hint. Hint 1 points to the named distinction; hint 2 points to the first correct step. After two ineffective hints show the prepared key, then pause if the fresh C1 response still fails. C1 checks the repaired component only and cannot replace a full independent check.

